IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poca-nouns`

-- Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Part 7, sections 330, 331 and 332 (failure to disclose) -- LAYER 1.   Target: main (checked on build 1.6.109).
-- Section 330 is the offence of a person in the regulated sector (a bank clerk, an accountant, a lawyer in a regulated business) who knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds
-- to know or suspect, that another person is laundering money and does not tell a nominated officer or the NCA.  Section 331 is the same offence for the nominated officer
-- who receives that disclosure and does not pass it on to the NCA; section 332 is the same for the nominated officers outside the regulated sector (disclosures under ss 337 and 338).
--
-- SHAPE.  Each condition is a function of facts the person can state.  The first, third and fourth conditions are BOOLEAN.
-- The second condition of s 330 depends on Schedule 9 (is the business in the regulated sector?), whose answer is MAYBE BOOLEAN, so the second condition is MAYBE BOOLEAN.
-- Each exception is a BOOLEAN; the offence composes them: an exception that applies is JUST FALSE ("But he does not commit an offence ... if"; a flat negative, ruling N2);
-- a condition that fails is JUST FALSE (lawyer-reading (a): a failed "if" is the text's no); a second condition that is NOTHING makes the offence NOTHING.
-- The duty to make the required disclosure is not stated as a duty: the text makes failing to do it an offence.  It is derived as a decision twin and a regulative rule (MUST, no WITHIN:
-- "as soon as is practicable" has no number, so the rule never breaches by the passing of time; the event of disclosing discharges it).
-- Facts that live in other instruments are inputs: the training specified by the Secretary of State's order (s 330(7)), the order about conduct lawful abroad, the Immigration Act 2014 checks,
-- the eligibility verification notice of the Social Security Administration Act 1992.

§ `Sections 330 to 332: failure to disclose`

§§ `s 330: the conditions`

-- src:124 | (2) The first condition is that he—
-- src:125 | (a) knows or suspects, or
-- src:126 | (b) has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting,
-- src:127 | that another person is engaged in money laundering.
@ref s 330(2) (src:124-127)
GIVEN `he knows or suspects that another person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that another person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(2) the first condition is satisfied` MEANS
    `he knows or suspects that another person is engaged in money laundering` OR `he has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that another person is engaged in money laundering`

-- src:128 | (3) The second condition is that the information or other matter—
-- src:129 | (a) on which his knowledge or suspicion is based, or
-- src:130 | (b) which gives reasonable grounds for such knowledge or suspicion,
-- src:131 | came to him in the course of a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 330(3) (src:128-131)
GIVEN `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2 for the business` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information or other matter on which his knowledge or suspicion is based, or which gives reasonable grounds for such knowledge or suspicion, came to him in the course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(3) the second condition is satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the information or other matter on which his knowledge or suspicion is based, or which gives reasonable grounds for such knowledge or suspicion, came to him in the course of that business`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that the information or other matter ... came to him in the course of a business in the regulated sector" (a failed condition read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2 for the business` -- Schedule 9 decides (s 330(12)); JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING pass through unchanged (NOTHING-kind, limited by its own wording, when Schedule 9 cannot say)

-- src:132 | (3A) The third condition is—
-- src:133 | (a) that he can identify the other person mentioned in subsection (2) or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property, or
-- src:134 | (b) that he believes, or it is reasonable to expect him to believe, that the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) will or may assist in identifying that other person or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property.
@ref s 330(3A) (src:132-134)
GIVEN `he can identify the other person mentioned in subsection (2) or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he believes, or it is reasonable to expect him to believe, that the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) will or may assist in identifying that other person or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(3A) the third condition is satisfied` MEANS
    `he can identify the other person mentioned in subsection (2) or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property` OR `he believes, or it is reasonable to expect him to believe, that the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) will or may assist in identifying that other person or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property`

-- src:135 | (4) The fourth condition is that he does not make the required disclosure to—
-- src:136 | (a) a nominated officer, or
-- src:137 | (b) a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency,
-- src:138 | as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) comes to him.
@ref s 330(4) (src:135-138)
GIVEN `he makes the required disclosure to a nominated officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he makes the required disclosure to a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he makes it as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) comes to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(4) the fourth condition is satisfied` MEANS
    NOT ((`he makes the required disclosure to a nominated officer` OR `he makes the required disclosure to a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency`) AND `he makes it as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) comes to him`)

-- src:139 | (5) The required disclosure is a disclosure of—
-- src:140 | (a) the identity of the other person mentioned in subsection (2), if he knows it,
-- src:141 | (b) the whereabouts of the laundered property, so far as he knows it, and
-- src:142 | (c) the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3).
@ref s 330(5) (src:139-142)
GIVEN `he knows the identity of the other person mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure gives the identity of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he knows the whereabouts of some or all of the laundered property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure gives the whereabouts of the laundered property, so far as he knows it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure gives the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(5) the disclosure is the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((NOT (`he knows the identity of the other person mentioned in subsection (2)`)) OR `the disclosure gives the identity of that person`)
           AND ((NOT (`he knows the whereabouts of some or all of the laundered property`)) OR `the disclosure gives the whereabouts of the laundered property, so far as he knows it`)
           AND `the disclosure gives the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The required disclosure is a disclosure of (a) the identity of the other person ..., if he knows it, (b) the whereabouts of the laundered property, so far as he knows it, and (c) the information or other matter" (a definition read as closed)

-- src:143 | (5A) The laundered property is the property forming the subject-matter of the money laundering that he knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that other person to be engaged in.
@ref s 330(5A) (src:143)
GIVEN `the property forms the subject-matter of the money laundering that he knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that other person to be engaged in` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(5A) the property is the laundered property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the property forms the subject-matter of the money laundering that he knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that other person to be engaged in` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The laundered property is the property forming the subject-matter of the money laundering" (a definition read as closed)

§§ `s 330: the exceptions`

-- src:145 | (a) he has a reasonable excuse for not making the required disclosure,
@ref s 330(6)(a) (src:145)
GIVEN `he has a reasonable excuse for not making the required disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(6)(a) the exception for a reasonable excuse applies` MEANS
    `he has a reasonable excuse for not making the required disclosure`

-- src:146 | (b) he is a professional legal adviser or ... relevant professional adviser and—
-- src:147 | (i) if he knows either of the things mentioned in subsection (5)(a) and (b), he knows the thing because of information or other matter that came to him in privileged circumstances, or
-- src:148 | (ii) the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) came to him in privileged circumstances, or
@ref s 330(6)(b) (src:146-148)
GIVEN `he is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he knows either of the things mentioned in subsection (5)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he knows the thing because of information or other matter that came to him in privileged circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) came to him in privileged circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(6)(b) the exception for a professional adviser applies` MEANS
        `he is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser`
    AND (    ((NOT (`he knows either of the things mentioned in subsection (5)(a) and (b)`)) OR `he knows the thing because of information or other matter that came to him in privileged circumstances`)
          OR `the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) came to him in privileged circumstances`)

-- src:149 | (c) subsection (7) or (7B) applies to him.
@ref s 330(6)(c) (src:149)
GIVEN `subsection (7) applies to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (7B) applies to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(6)(c) subsection (7) or (7B) applies to him` MEANS
    `subsection (7) applies to him` OR `subsection (7B) applies to him`

-- src:150 | (7) This subsection applies to a person if—
-- src:151 | (a) he does not know or suspect that another person is engaged in money laundering, and
-- src:152 | (b) he has not been provided by his employer with such training as is specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 330(7) (src:150-152)
GIVEN `he does not know or suspect that another person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has been provided by his employer with such training as is specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(7) the exception for an untrained person who does not know or suspect applies` MEANS
    `he does not know or suspect that another person is engaged in money laundering` AND (NOT (`he has been provided by his employer with such training as is specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of this section`))

-- src:153 | (7B) This subsection applies to a person if—
-- src:154 | (a) he is employed by, or is in partnership with, a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser to provide the adviser with assistance or support,
-- src:155 | (b) the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) comes to the person in connection with the provision of such assistance or support, and
-- src:156 | (c) the information or other matter came to the adviser in privileged circumstances.
@ref s 330(7B) (src:153-156)
GIVEN `he is employed by, or is in partnership with, a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser to provide the adviser with assistance or support` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) comes to the person in connection with the provision of such assistance or support` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information or other matter came to the adviser in privileged circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(7B) the exception for a person assisting an adviser applies` MEANS
    `he is employed by, or is in partnership with, a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser to provide the adviser with assistance or support`
    AND `the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) comes to the person in connection with the provision of such assistance or support`
    AND `the information or other matter came to the adviser in privileged circumstances`

-- src:157 | (7C) Nor does a person commit an offence under this section if—
-- src:158 | (a) he knows, or believes on reasonable grounds, that the money laundering is occurring in a particular country or territory outside the United Kingdom, and
-- src:159 | (b) the money laundering—
-- src:160 | (i) is not unlawful under the criminal law applying in that country or territory, and
-- src:161 | (ii) is not of a description prescribed in an order made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 330(7C) (src:157-161)
GIVEN `he knows, or believes on reasonable grounds, that the money laundering is occurring in a particular country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money laundering is not unlawful under the criminal law applying in that country or territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money laundering is of a description prescribed in an order made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(7C) the exception for money laundering lawful abroad applies` MEANS
    `he knows, or believes on reasonable grounds, that the money laundering is occurring in a particular country or territory outside the United Kingdom`
    AND `the money laundering is not unlawful under the criminal law applying in that country or territory`
    AND (NOT (`the money laundering is of a description prescribed in an order made by the Secretary of State`))

-- src:162 | (7D) Nor does a person commit an offence under this section if—
-- src:163 | (a) the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) consists of or includes information that was obtained only in consequence of the carrying out of a status check under section 40 of the Immigration Act 2014 or an immigration check under section 40A of that Act or both, and
-- src:164 | (b) but for the information so obtained the person would not have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that another person is engaged in money laundering.
@ref s 330(7D) (src:162-164)
GIVEN `the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) consists of or includes information that was obtained only in consequence of the carrying out of a status check under section 40 of the Immigration Act 2014 or an immigration check under section 40A of that Act or both` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for the information so obtained the person would not have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that another person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(7D) the exception for information from an immigration check applies` MEANS
    `the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) consists of or includes information that was obtained only in consequence of the carrying out of a status check under section 40 of the Immigration Act 2014 or an immigration check under section 40A of that Act or both`
    AND `but for the information so obtained the person would not have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that another person is engaged in money laundering`

-- src:165 | (7E) Nor does a person commit an offence under this section if—
-- src:166 | (a) the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) consists of or includes information that was obtained only in consequence of complying with an eligibility verification notice given to the person under paragraph 1(1) of Schedule 3B to the Social Security Administration Act 1992, and
-- src:167 | (b) but for the information so obtained the person would not know or suspect, or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that another person is engaged in money laundering.
@ref s 330(7E) (src:165-167)
GIVEN `the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) consists of or includes information that was obtained only in consequence of complying with an eligibility verification notice given to the person under paragraph 1(1) of Schedule 3B to the Social Security Administration Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for the information so obtained the person would not know or suspect, or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that another person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(7E) the exception for information from an eligibility verification notice applies` MEANS
    `the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) consists of or includes information that was obtained only in consequence of complying with an eligibility verification notice given to the person under paragraph 1(1) of Schedule 3B to the Social Security Administration Act 1992`
    AND `but for the information so obtained the person would not know or suspect, or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that another person is engaged in money laundering`

-- src:144 | (6) But he does not commit an offence under this section if—
@ref s 330(6) (src:144)
GIVEN `the exception for a reasonable excuse applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for a professional adviser applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (7) or (7B) applies to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for money laundering lawful abroad applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for information from an immigration check applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for information from an eligibility verification notice applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(6) to (7E) one of the exceptions applies` MEANS
        `the exception for a reasonable excuse applies`
     OR `the exception for a professional adviser applies`
     OR `subsection (7) or (7B) applies to him`
     OR `the exception for money laundering lawful abroad applies`
     OR `the exception for information from an immigration check applies`
     OR `the exception for information from an eligibility verification notice applies`

§§ `s 330: the offence, the duty and the court's guidance`

-- src:123 | (1) A person commits an offence if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are satisfied.
@ref s 330(1) (src:123)
GIVEN `the first condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second condition is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the third condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fourth condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the exceptions applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `one of the exceptions applies` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But he does not commit an offence under this section if" and "Nor does a person commit an offence under this section if"
        IF NOT (`the first condition is satisfied` AND `the third condition is satisfied` AND `the fourth condition is satisfied`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are satisfied" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE `the second condition is satisfied` -- JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE or NOTHING as the second condition says (NOTHING-kind, limited by its own wording, when Schedule 9 cannot say)

@ref s 330(1) (src:123)
GIVEN `the first condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second condition is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the third condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the exceptions applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(1) the person must make the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `one of the exceptions applies` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty is derived from the offence, and "he does not commit an offence under this section if" removes it (derived, not stated: marginal reading (b))
        IF NOT (`the first condition is satisfied` AND `the third condition is satisfied`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the offence needs "the conditions in subsections (2) to (4)" (a failed condition read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE `the second condition is satisfied` -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING as the second condition says

@ref s 330(4) (src:135-138)
GIVEN `the answer under section 330(1): the person must make the required disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 330(4) the person must make the required disclosure to a nominated officer or an authorised person as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF `the answer under section 330(1): the person must make the required disclosure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         MUST `make the required disclosure`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 330(4): the required disclosure was not made to a nominated officer or a person authorised by the Director General of the National Crime Agency as soon as practicable"
    ELSE FULFILLED -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): when the duty is JUST FALSE, or the text cannot say (NOTHING), the text states nothing the person must do

-- src:168 | (8) In deciding whether a person committed an offence under this section the court must consider whether he followed any relevant guidance which was at the time concerned—
-- src:169 | (a) issued by a supervisory authority or any other appropriate body,
-- src:170 | (b) approved by the Treasury, and
-- src:171 | (c) published in a manner it approved as appropriate in its opinion to bring the guidance to the attention of persons likely to be affected by it.
@ref s 330(8) (src:168-171)
GIVEN `the guidance was issued by a supervisory authority or any other appropriate body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance was approved by the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance was published in a manner the Treasury approved as appropriate in its opinion to bring the guidance to the attention of persons likely to be affected by it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance was in force at the time concerned and is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(8) the court must consider whether he followed the guidance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the guidance was issued by a supervisory authority or any other appropriate body` AND `the guidance was approved by the Treasury` AND `the guidance was published in a manner the Treasury approved as appropriate in its opinion to bring the guidance to the attention of persons likely to be affected by it` AND `the guidance was in force at the time concerned and is relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the court must consider "any relevant guidance which was at the time concerned" issued, approved and published as stated; the text does not say the court may not consider other guidance

§§ `s 330: nominated officer, privileged circumstances and the defined terms`

-- src:172 | (9) A disclosure to a nominated officer is a disclosure which—
-- src:173 | (a) is made to a person nominated by the alleged offender’s employer to receive disclosures under this section, and
-- src:174 | (b) is made in the course of the alleged offender’s employment ....
@ref s 330(9) (src:172-174)
GIVEN `it is made to a person nominated by the alleged offender's employer to receive disclosures under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made in the course of the alleged offender's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 330(9) the disclosure satisfies paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition of a disclosure to a nominated officer` MEANS
    `it is made to a person nominated by the alleged offender's employer to receive disclosures under this section` AND `it is made in the course of the alleged offender's employment`

-- src:175 | (9A) But a disclosure which satisfies paragraphs (a) and (b) of subsection (9) is not to be taken as a disclosure to a nominated officer if the person making the disclosure—
-- src:176 | (a) is a professional legal adviseror ... relevant professional adviser,
-- src:177 | (b) makes it for the purpose of obtaining advice about making a disclosure under this section, and
-- src:178 | (c) does not intend it to be a disclosure under this section.
@ref s 330(9A) (src:175-178)
GIVEN `the disclosure satisfies paragraphs (a) and (b) of subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making the disclosure is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he makes it for the purpose of obtaining advice about making a disclosure under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he does not intend it to be a disclosure under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(9A) the disclosure is a disclosure to a nominated officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the disclosure satisfies paragraphs (a) and (b) of subsection (9)`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure to a nominated officer is a disclosure which (a) is made to a person nominated ... and (b) is made in the course of the alleged offender's employment" (a definition read as closed)
        IF `the person making the disclosure is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` AND `he makes it for the purpose of obtaining advice about making a disclosure under this section` AND `he does not intend it to be a disclosure under this section` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not to be taken as a disclosure to a nominated officer if"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:179 | (10) Information or other matter comes to a professional legal adviser or ... relevant professional adviser in privileged circumstances if it is communicated or given to him—
-- src:180 | (a) by (or by a representative of) a client of his in connection with the giving by the adviser of legal advice to the client,
-- src:181 | (b) by (or by a representative of) a person seeking legal advice from the adviser, or
-- src:182 | (c) by a person in connection with legal proceedings or contemplated legal proceedings.
-- src:183 | (11) But subsection (10) does not apply to information or other matter which is communicated or given with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose.
@ref s 330(10) (src:179-183)
GIVEN `it is communicated or given to him by (or by a representative of) a client of his in connection with the giving by the adviser of legal advice to the client` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is communicated or given to him by (or by a representative of) a person seeking legal advice from the adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is communicated or given to him by a person in connection with legal proceedings or contemplated legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is communicated or given with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(10) the information or other matter came to the adviser in privileged circumstances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is communicated or given with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But subsection (10) does not apply to information or other matter which is communicated or given with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose"
        IF `it is communicated or given to him by (or by a representative of) a client of his in connection with the giving by the adviser of legal advice to the client` OR `it is communicated or given to him by (or by a representative of) a person seeking legal advice from the adviser` OR `it is communicated or given to him by a person in connection with legal proceedings or contemplated legal proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "comes to a professional legal adviser or ... relevant professional adviser in privileged circumstances if it is communicated or given to him" in the three ways listed (an "if" list read as closed: marginal reading (a))

@ref s 330(12)(a) (src:184-186)
GIVEN `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(12)(a) the business is a business in the regulated sector` MEANS
    `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2` -- Schedule 9 decides; JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING pass through unchanged

-- src:184 | (12) Schedule 9 has effect for the purpose of determining what is—
-- src:185 | (a) a business in the regulated sector;
-- src:186 | (b) a supervisory authority.
@ref s 330(12)(b) (src:184-186)
GIVEN `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraph 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(12)(b) the body is a supervisory authority` MEANS
    `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraph 4` -- Schedule 9 decides; JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING pass through unchanged

-- src:187 | (13) An appropriate body is any body which regulates or is representative of any trade, profession, business or employment carried on by the alleged offender.
@ref s 330(13) (src:187)
GIVEN `it regulates or is representative of a trade, profession, business or employment carried on by the alleged offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(13) the body is an appropriate body` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it regulates or is representative of a trade, profession, business or employment carried on by the alleged offender` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appropriate body is any body which regulates or is representative of any trade, profession, business or employment carried on by the alleged offender"

-- src:188 | (14) A relevant professional adviser is an accountant, auditor or tax adviser who is a member of a professional body which is established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers (as the case may be) and which makes provision for—
-- src:189 | (a) testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership of such a body as a condition for such admission; and
-- src:190 | (b) imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members, as well as imposing sanctions for non-compliance with those standards.
@ref s 330(14) (src:188-190)
GIVEN a IS A `Adviser`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(14) the person is a relevant professional adviser` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a's `accountant, auditor or tax adviser` AND a's `member of a professional body established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers` AND a's `the body makes provision for testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership as a condition for such admission` AND (a's `the body makes provision for imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members` AND a's `the body makes provision for imposing sanctions for non-compliance with those standards`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant professional adviser is an accountant, auditor or tax adviser who is a member of a professional body which is established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers ... and which makes provision for (a) ... and (b) ..." (a definition read as closed)

§§ `s 331: nominated officers in the regulated sector`

-- src:193 | (2) The first condition is that he—
