-- src:201 | (3A) The third condition is—
-- src:202 | (a) that he knows the identity of the other person mentioned in subsection (2), or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property, in consequence of a disclosure made under section 330,
-- src:203 | (b) that that other person, or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property, can be identified from the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3), or
-- src:204 | (c) that he believes, or it is reasonable to expect him to believe, that the information or other matter will or may assist in identifying that other person or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property.
@ref s 331(3A) (src:201-204)
GIVEN `he knows the identity of the other person mentioned in subsection (2), or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property, in consequence of a disclosure made under section 330` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that other person, or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property, can be identified from the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he believes, or it is reasonable to expect him to believe, that the information or other matter will or may assist in identifying that other person or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 331(3A) the third condition is satisfied` MEANS
    `he knows the identity of the other person mentioned in subsection (2), or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property, in consequence of a disclosure made under section 330`
    OR `that other person, or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property, can be identified from the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3)`
    OR `he believes, or it is reasonable to expect him to believe, that the information or other matter will or may assist in identifying that other person or the whereabouts of any of the laundered property`

-- src:205 | (4) The fourth condition is that he does not make the required disclosure to a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) comes to him.
@ref s 331(4) (src:205)
GIVEN `he makes the required disclosure to a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he makes it as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) comes to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 331(4) the fourth condition is satisfied` MEANS
    NOT (`he makes the required disclosure to a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency` AND `he makes it as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3) comes to him`)

-- src:206 | (5) The required disclosure is a disclosure of—
-- src:207 | (a) the identity of the other person mentioned in subsection (2), if disclosed to him under section 330,
-- src:208 | (b) the whereabouts of the laundered property, so far as disclosed to him under section 330, and
-- src:209 | (c) the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3).
@ref s 331(5) (src:206-209)
GIVEN `the identity of the other person was disclosed to him under section 330` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure gives that identity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the whereabouts of some or all of the laundered property were disclosed to him under section 330` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure gives the whereabouts so far as disclosed to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure gives the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 331(5) the disclosure is the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((NOT (`the identity of the other person was disclosed to him under section 330`)) OR `the disclosure gives that identity`)
           AND ((NOT (`the whereabouts of some or all of the laundered property were disclosed to him under section 330`)) OR `the disclosure gives the whereabouts so far as disclosed to him`)
           AND `the disclosure gives the information or other matter mentioned in subsection (3)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The required disclosure is a disclosure of (a) the identity of the other person ..., if disclosed to him under section 330, (b) the whereabouts ..., so far as disclosed to him ... and (c) the information or other matter" (a definition read as closed)

