-- src:192 | (1) A person nominated to receive disclosures under section 330 commits an offence if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are satisfied.
@ref s 331(1) (src:192)
GIVEN `he is a person nominated to receive disclosures under section 330` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fourth condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for a reasonable excuse applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for money laundering lawful abroad applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for information from an immigration check applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for information from an eligibility verification notice applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 331(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the exception for a reasonable excuse applies` OR `the exception for money laundering lawful abroad applies` OR `the exception for information from an immigration check applies` OR `the exception for information from an eligibility verification notice applies` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But he does not commit an offence under this section if" and "Nor does a person commit an offence under this section if"
        IF NOT (`he is a person nominated to receive disclosures under section 330` AND `the first condition is satisfied` AND `the second condition is satisfied` AND `the third condition is satisfied` AND `the fourth condition is satisfied`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person nominated to receive disclosures under section 330 commits an offence if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are satisfied" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 331(1) (src:192)
GIVEN `he is a person nominated to receive disclosures under section 330` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the exceptions applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 331(1) the nominated officer must make the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `one of the exceptions applies` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty is derived from the offence, and "he does not commit an offence under this section if" removes it (derived, not stated: marginal reading (b))
        IF NOT (`he is a person nominated to receive disclosures under section 330` AND `the first condition is satisfied` AND `the second condition is satisfied` AND `the third condition is satisfied`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the offence needs "the conditions in subsections (2) to (4)" (a failed condition read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 331(4) (src:205)
GIVEN `the answer under section 331(1): the nominated officer must make the required disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 331(4) the nominated officer must make the required disclosure to an authorised person as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF `the answer under section 331(1): the nominated officer must make the required disclosure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the nominated officer`
         MUST `make the required disclosure`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the nominated officer` BECAUSE "s 331(4): the required disclosure was not made to a person authorised by the Director General of the National Crime Agency as soon as practicable"
    ELSE FULFILLED -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): when the duty is JUST FALSE, the text states nothing the nominated officer must do

